@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] ground-is-the-rendered-surface
Every placed instance (trees, bushes, rocks, props, buildings, signs, paths) MUST be seated on the surface
that is rendered and collided at its point: the final stage of the product that owns that footprint. It
MUST NOT sample a natural, pre-carve, hidden, superseded, coarse or neighbouring surface, nor the max/min of
several. Where products overlap, the footprint's owner is the ground. An instance MUST rest within its
declared embedding of that surface: never floating above it and never buried beyond the embedding.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] seamless-surface-boundaries
Wherever two ground or walkable surfaces meet (region and region, fine terrain and backdrop, city and
mountains, terrain and paving, terrain and a shore or water edge), the boundary MUST have one owner. The
other side MUST meet the owner's exact edge profile at that edge, fading over a declared margin, from the
same function and samples on both sides: no vertical step, slit, sliver or overlap along the seam. A
coarse surface MUST carry vertices or knots where the fine edge bends. A skirt, apron or wall MAY close an
intended height change, but MUST NOT hide an unexplained mismatch. Adding or moving a boundary MUST add a
test that samples both sides along the whole edge and asserts the mismatch is zero within float tolerance.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] closed-visible-geometry
Geometry that any reachable camera can see from more than one side MUST be closed or explicitly two-sided
with thickness. That covers roofs, eaves, awnings, canopies, decks, bridges, stairs, balconies, signs and
walls seen from below or behind. A one-sided sheet MUST face away from every viewpoint that can see its back.
Roofs MUST seat on their walls with no gap, with soffits and gable infill closing them from below. Faces
MUST wind outward consistently, so that back-face culling never removes a visible side.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] pieces-meet-by-construction
Adjoining built pieces MUST meet by construction. That covers treads and risers, landings, walls and roofs,
paving and kerbs, platforms and their skirts, bridges and abutments, and modules and their neighbours.
Their shared edges MUST come from one plan or shared coordinates, not from separately tuned offsets: no
open gap, floating slab, daylight under a step or nosing, or coplanar overlap that flickers. A piece that
stands on the ground MUST reach below the ground it stands on, wherever that ground is lower.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] walkable-routes-traversable
Every route the player is meant to walk (stairs, ramps, paths, landings and their joins to streets,
terraces and doors) MUST be traversable by the character in both directions without jumping. Each rise
MUST be well under the character's step height, with treads at least a footstep deep. Slopes MUST stay
under the walkable floor angle. There MUST be no gap or lip at either end. A new or rebuilt route MUST be
validated by driving the character over it in game both ways; ray traces or plan checks alone are not enough.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] visual-defects-get-regression-checks
A fix for a reported visual or traversal defect (hole, slit, gap, floating or buried object, invisible
face, impassable step) MUST add an automated check that fails on the original defect. The check MUST be
written against the general rule above it (a seam sampler, a grounding check, a closure check), so it
also covers the next region or feature of the same kind. Evidence MUST name the source revision it ran on.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture] one-implementation-per-mechanism
A shared world mechanism MUST have one implementation that every region reuses rather than copies. That
covers terrain products and queries, seam stitching, grounding, mesh builders and their closed primitives,
stairs and paving, foliage placement and LOD export. A region MUST keep its own data, layout and
generators in its own region directory (Yorimichi: games/yorimichi/world/regions/<region>/). It MUST change another region's output only through that
region's published products or declared boundary APIs, never by patching its code paths, meshes,
materials or placements from outside. A height or ground function MUST serve every consumer of that ground
(mesh, collision, placement and checks) rather than being re-derived per consumer.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:performance] edits-rebuild-locally
An edit to one region, asset or feature MUST rebuild only the products that actually read it. Steps MUST
declare their own code, the shared modules and products they read, and spatial queries for neighbour reads,
following docs/WORLD_BUILD_PRACTICES.md. They MUST NOT declare whole directories, other regions' code or
global catalogues they do not consume. Terrain consumers MUST read published terrain products or narrow
kernels rather than importing a whole generator, so that unrelated work does not change their keys. Generation
MUST be deterministic, with stable IDs and randomness seeded per region, asset and purpose, so that unchanged
inputs reproduce identical outputs. A recipe change that widens the rebuild scope MUST report its measured
effect (atelier build --changes and --timings) in its PR.
